 "method": "The county clerk's office e-mailed, on 2026-11-18, a page of a 2026 Mapping Solutions plat book, \"Political Townships and Commissioners' Districts Map\", with the line between the 1st and 2nd Commissioner's Districts drawn on it in blue. The page is that publisher's copyrighted work and is not kept here; its SHA-256 is scanSha256. The line runs along township lines but in Lorance township, which it splits: Union, Whitewater, Crooked Creek and Scopus townships are whole in the Second District and Filmore, Liberty and Wayne whole in the First, and each of their Census 2020 blocks is listed under its township's district. In Lorance the blue line was read off the page, the page having been lined up with six of the Census Bureau's township corners (an affine fit, about 22 m to a pixel) and then moved 6 pixels east, where the Census Bureau's city limits of Marble Hill match the page's, and each of Lorance's 204 blocks was put in the district holding most of it. About 1.5 km of the line, in Marble Hill, runs under the printed township label and was read from the parts of it that show between the letters. North and south of Marble Hill the traced line runs where the Census Bureau's 2020 line between the Marble Hill and Lutesville voting districts runs; in the town it runs farther east, so 24 blocks with 304 people in the 2020 Marble Hill voting district are in the First District. The line crosses one block with 91 people (290179502002006), which is in the First District, where 65% of its area lies.",
